---------- SUMMARY -----------

-- You could call this the Path Access Review patch because that's the main thing. Basically I went through all the vanilla MA nations and looked at their levels of access in different paths via recruitment, whether they e.g. can reasonably get a F3 or S3 caster just by recruiting. I then compared this with the Warhammer nations and saw that in general I had been providing too broad a level of path access and that there were some specifically egregious cases. So this Path Access Review resulted in me changing the paths on quite a few mages. I may go further in the future, but this is a good start I feel. Overall levels of magic were mostly left untouched, so a mage with 6 levels of magic still has 6, they just might not be able to get to level 2 or 3 in a certain path. Often this might actually improve the mage, by making their paths less broad.

