	-- Ogre Hunter gold cost increased 140 -> 150 (more in line with vanilla prices, slight nerf to gold/research efficiency)

-- SKAVEN
	--SKRYRE
	-- Warlock Engineer gold cost increased 290 -> 300 (tiny nerf)
	-- Poison Wind Globadier recruitment limit increased 3 -> 5 per month
	-- Poison Wind Mortar recruitment limit increased 1 -> 2 per month
	-- Poison Wind Mortar poison damage increased 6 -> 7, aoe increased slightly, now fires once every other round (overall a slight nerf)
	-- Doomflayer recruitment limit increased 1 -> 2 per month
	-- Doomflayer blades base damage 6 -> 7 (they were intended to really mangle smaller things, now they do I think)
	-- Warpfire Thrower recruitment limit increased 1 -> 2 per month
	-- Warpfire Thrower aoe inreased 2 -> 3, damage reduced by 1, fires once every other round (a slight nerf overall)
	-- Warplightning Thrower now ignores shields, fires 6 projectiles not 5, only fires every other round (maybe a slight nerf overall?)
	-- Warplightning Thrower recruitment limit increased 1 -> 2 per month
	--MOULDER
	-- Giant Rat now recruitable from forts
	-- Rat Ogre rags upgraded to leather straps (fitting, slight buff to prot)
	-- Mutators no longer have magic paths, or douse, but have an item to autocasts ferocity each round
	-- Mutator gold cost decreased considerably
	-- Mutator now summons 1 Giant Wolfrat per month
	-- Throt, being a mutator, also loses magic paths, gains autocast item (of higher quality)
	-- Skweel gets the same autocast item as mutators
	-- Packmasters get a weaker version of the mutator autocast item
	-- Packmaster gold cost increased from 70 -> 80 (because of the autocast item)
	-- All moulder summons removed (will be replaced with something to allow Moulder to procure beasties)
	--OTHERS
	-- Queek bodyguards now Crimson Guard, not mere Stormvermin
	-- Pox Rat summon morale decreased 30 -> 12 (the pretender mount version has 30, this was never intended for the summon)
	-- Pox Rat size 7 -> 6
	-- Verminlord sprite redrawn to be a bit bigger, size 6 -> 7, +3 hp (he was looking rather puny compared with recent Greater Daemon sprites)
	-- Keeper of the Pillar pretender no longer available as a god (I never liked this pretender, didn't feel like redrawing the sprite, and maybe I'll do more specific verminlords in the future)
	
-- SLAANESH
	-- Poison resistance on various daemons reduced from 10 -> 5 (more in line with dominions, makes poison somewhat of a threat against them)
	-- Note about demonic mount added to hellstrider
	-- Added spell to summon 3 chaos spawn at once

-- TILEA
	-- grudgebringers will no longer always turn up as the first RoR
	
-- TOMB KINGS
	-- Fires resistance values increased on warsphinx and crew (it's sad if warsphinxes accidentally kill each others crew)
	
-- TZEENTCH
	-- Cultist now costs a holy point
	-- Poison resistance on various daemons reduced from 10 -> 5 (more in line with dominions, makes poison somewhat of a threat against them)




-- version 1.31

---------- NEW CONTENT ------------

-- DARK ELVES
	-- Added Scourgerunner Chariot as recruitable troop

-- HIGH ELVES
	-- Added Tiranoc Ithilmar Chariot as recruitable troop
	-- Added Tyrion the Defender of Ulthuan as a luck independent hero

---------- CHANGES ------------

-- GENERAL
	-- More troops/commanders given clothes or rags prot 2 armour where appropriate
	-- Starting armies made more equal in terms of total resource and gold cost
	
-- CATHAY
	-- Immortal Iron Dragon size fixed
-- DARK ELVES
	-- Various mages of significant authority given limited sailing (partly so they don't get stranded, partly thematic for this naval power nation)
-- HIGH ELVES
	-- Magic attuned researcher removed entirely from the nation (this was very swingy, probably too strong, and thematically not the best fit)
	-- War Lions get gold collar very light barding
	-- Shadow Walker added to non-fort recruitment
	-- Shadow Warrior recpoint cost reduced somewhat (was a bit too hard to ever foreign recruit them)
	-- Ellyrian Reaver recpoint cost redcued somewhat (same reason as shadow warrior)
	-- Ellyrian Reaver and Noble now recruitable outside of forts (their description indicated this would be reasonable)
	-- Rangers now recruitable only in forests and mountains and forts (instead of everywhere, a thematic restriction)
	-- Silverin Guard spear defence malus removed (this was a feature of the long spear weapon, but seems too harsh)
	-- Various mages of significant authority given limited sailing (partly so they don't get stranded, partly thematic for this naval power nation)
	-- Tiranoc prince sprite updated, given ithilmar barding for mount (mostly because it's cool, also so they can thug more)
	-- Removed fear from Eltharion (his mount has it)
	-- Protective Presence spell now nextspells Dome of Arcane Warding correctly
	-- Shadow Walker gets 25 Darkvision (same as troops)
	-- Storm Weaver mage now coast forts only (thematic mainly, slight nerf)
	-- gold cost of dragon mage reduced slightly
	-- White Lions, War Lions, and White Lion chariots now only recruitable from mountain forts (thematic, cutting the roster down a bit in most forts)
	-- White Lion reclimit raised from 5 -> 10 (now they are terrain restricted, less important to flat restrict them)
-- KHORNE
	-- Scylla got his claws back
-- KISLEV
	-- War Bears get studded collar very light barding
	-- Ungol Crones older (were too young to be crones)
	-- Ungol Lancer def base 11 -> 10 (were perhaps a bit too good for the cost)
-- LIZARDMEN
	-- Stegadon crew given more ammo for their poisoned javelins and spears to stab with (general buff, makes them more interesting)
	-- Some troops and commanders got small ceremonial plates armour (a slight buff, some extra resource cost, helps with amour interaction effects)
-- MIDDENHEIM
	-- Hunting hound recruitment limit description fixed
-- NORSCA
	-- Throgg given tight rein ability (leader of trolls after all)
	-- Added some explicit descriptions for sailing abilities
	-- Raven/Bear/Wolfstruck Jarls and Chiefs given relevant sailing abilities (to avoid them getting stranded mostly)
-- SKAVEN
	-- Doom flayer weapon split into 2 so it can hit 2 targets per round (better vs mobs)
	-- Assassination event can no longer target eshin assassin (always intended to work this way)
	-- chain cuirass armour for Boneripper (a buff for the big dumb brute)
	-- Twiceborn now gives a sensible result for Cauldron of a Thousands Poxes and Screaming Bell (used to create titanic wights, which was silly)
-- TOMB KINGS
	-- Additional crew of Warsphinx got invuln 10, fire res 5 (helping with survivability)




