#descr "Har Ganeth is the spiritual centre of Khaine's worship, with many shrines to the God of Murder and a skyline dominated by the massive Great Temple of Khaine. It is from Har Ganeth that Hellebron rules over the Witch Elves and countless slaves are brought to the city to be sacrificed to Khaine. Many of these sacrifices are performed by the Witch Elves and Death Hags, but after particularly great victories Har Ganeth hosts ritual mass executions in which prisoners of war are decapitated and their heads cast down the steps of the Great Temple. These executions are performed by the feared Executioners of Har Ganeth, whose loyalty is to the city and to Khaine rather than the reigning Crone Hellebron. Executioners have embraced discipline and efficiency, seeing the excesses and cruelty of the Witch Elves as needless and indulgent; a poor tribute to the true will of the God of Murder. Each Executioner strides to battle well armoured, their face hidden behind a skull like visage, and armed with a long two handed blade known as a Draich, the ceremonial weapon of his calling. Each Draich is subtly different, tailored and refined to the exact skills and preferences of its wielder, but each is as deadly as the next in the hands of its master. Executioners are truly devoted to Khaine in their cold, efficient manner and are considered sacred warriors of Khaine by the populace."
