#descr "Trolls are hulking creatures whose hunched appearance belies their powerful nature. These dim witted creatures are eternally hungry and will consume almost anything from rocks and plants to metal or flesh. Not surprisingly their stomachs contain extremely powerful acids which they are known to spontaneously vomit at prey in lieu of beating it to a pulp with a crude club or tearing it apart with their long claws. Trolls are incredibly strong and, though they are quite slow and uncoordinated, truly deadly opponents in battle, but their greatest strength is their ability to regenerate. Trolls can heal any wound entirely in short order and even in the course of seconds or minutes their flesh will knit back together, making the task of killing them very difficult. River Trolls are primarily found anywhere there are marshes, bogs, or rivers for them to predate and make their lairs within. River Trolls lack the resistance to magic and very tough hides of Stone Trolls, but are well adapted to their common environment and capable of secreting a sticky and foul-smelling slime which can greatly hinder any attacking foe. They are also known to be more aggressive and slightly slower witted than their mountain dwelling cousins. Without the help of Shamanic rituals River Trolls can only reliably be found in swamps and it is fairly rare for the Greenskins to be able to get them to join their armies. On the plus side River Trolls are too stupid to require any payment beyond food.

