---- WELCOME EVENT

#newevent
#msg "Skavenblight special mechanics explainer:

Warpstone Seams. Each turn in any Skaven province there is a chance a Warpstone Seam will be discovered; a site which grants 1 fire, 1 earth, and 1 death gem and increases unrest. There can only be one Warpstone Seam per province and each turn there's a chance it will become Exhausted (more likely if province no longer Skaven controlled). Exhausted Seams don't give gems or unrest, but prevent a Warpstone Seam being found there. Exhausted Seams controlled by Skaven have a chance each turn to become a Warpstone Seam again if a lab present, though the lab may be destroyed in the process, or even destroyed without restoring the site.

Clan Pacts. Each forted province you control other than your cap may be supported by a powerful Clan. This support comes as a site and is triggered by the presence of a Moulder Mutator, Pestilens Plague Priest, Skryre Warlock Engineer, Eshin Assassin, or Warlord. In the case of the Warlord there is an equal chance of Mors or Rictus support. For AI players it's random, no commander required.

Gnawing Rats. Your nation naturally spreads a great swarm of Gnawing Rats beyond its borders. These Rats consume supplies (200), increase unrest (4), and occasionally (5%) eat some PD or try (2%) to eat a commander. Any non-Skaven province adjacent to one of yours has a 20% chance of infestation each turn. Each province adjacent to an infested one has an 6% chance each turn to be infested. ~10 PD grants a good chance to remove the Rats, while ~15 PD for Skaven or ~20 for non-skaven grants relative immunity. 50% chance to make 2d6 rat troops if in a Skaven province. There is additional 40% chance for removal in any AI prov."
#req_owncapital 1
#nolog
#req_pregame 1 -- only happens before the first turn of the game
#req_fornation 158 -- skaven
#nation 158 -- skaven
#rarity 5
#header 2 -- use the first line of the event as the header
#end


