#descr "Ruglud was once the second in command of the Crooked Eyes, a mid-sized Orc tribe with the extreme misfortune of angering the Infernal Legion Azgorh. Their numbers cut down to barely a few score by the Chaos Dwarfs, the Crooked Eyes found themselves trapped in the ruins of a remote Dwarfhold, surrounded on all sides by hobgoblin archers. Each time the Orcs tried to break their way out they lost more to a hail of arrows and were forced to retreat. Humiliated and enraged, the Big Boss of the Crooked Eyes lashed out and struck Ruglud, sending him tumbling into a stone wall headfirst. This act had two consequences; firstly the impact with the stone wall jarred something permanently loose in Ruglud's brain, instantly filling it with new notions, and secondly the wall collapsed, revealing a hidden cache of Dwarf crossbows and armour. Ruglud promptly picked up one of the crossbows and put a bolt between the eyes of his former Big Boss, killing him instantly. With a sudden authority he then ordered the Orcs to clad themselves in a patchwork of Dwarf armour, each pick up a crossbow, and shoot their way out of the Hobgoblin trap. Many of the Crooked Eyes refused but those that followed Ruglud so shocked their enemies that they were able to break free and head west. Since that time Ruglud and any Orc crazy enough to follow his bizarre ways have made a living as the mercenary band known only as Ruglud's Armoured Orcs.

