#name "King of Kings"
#descr "Settra the Imperishable is the King of all Tomb Kings, a ruthless leader in life whose unyielding desire for conquest and glory led him to create perhaps the most powerful kingdom the mortal world has ever known. Settra wished nothing more than total dominion over the world and while his power grew and more realms fell to his armies he became increasingly bitter, for he knew he would eventually be defeated, not by any mortal but by the end of his own lifespan. So it was that Settra founded the Mortuary Cult to seek immortality for their King and when it became clear they would not complete their task within his life, had the impossibly vast Pyramid of Settra constructed as his tomb, so that when their knowledge met his ambition they could restore him. When Settra was finally awakened it was as a cursed undead creature, incredibly powerful and near immortal, but not in the true paradise that was promised. Settra quickly set about dominating the lesser warring Tomb Kings and established a new Nehekhara, a land of the dead, vowing revenge on the mortals that had plundered his ancient lands and above all else on Nagash, the traitor who had brought about the curse. Settra rides into war atop his chariot which bears the blessings of all the ancient Nehekharan gods and whose wheels glow with unearthly power, upon his brow rests the Crown of Nehekhara which amplifies his already legendary ability to command, around his neck hangs the Scarab Broach of Usirian which protects him from hostile magic, and in his hand he carries the Blade of Ptra, an eternal blade augmented with the power of the sun. Though hiw great power makes it very unlikely, should Settra ever be struck down within the dominion of Nehekhara he will surely in time arise once more to enact his revenge. As the King of Kings Settra holds ultimate religious authority and is tantamount to a God himself, in addition to understanding the basics of the magic used by the Mortuary Cult."
