#descr "Within every Vampire there exists a ravenous, insatiable monster driven to feed on the blood of the living. Each Bloodline has found its own methods to keep control of this nature and to establish the Vampire as master of their own fate, at least to some degree, whether it is through martial honour, pursuit of arcane knowledge, decadent indulgence, aristocratic status, or simply channeling their animalistic desires into bursts of wanton violence. Yet there are some Vampires that, in time, give in to their baser nature and allow the slavering monster of destruction to fully emerge, permanently changing their form; these Vampires become the creatures known as Varghulfs. Varghulfs are hulking monsters with chiropteran features that kill and destroy without pause and have no concern for the trappings of civilisation, though one should never mistake them for mindless or dumb beasts, for they retain all their sharp cunning and their predatory instincts are stronger than ever. Varghulfs have no interest in leading others or amassing worldly power and as they are despised and often destroyed by their civilised cousins, they typically seek to join the forces of a powerful Vampire of the Carstein or Strigoi Bloodline, those with a familiar bestial nature under the surface, for protection or simply the chance to luxuriate in carnage. In battle a Varghulf is a terrifying force coupling incredible strength and speed with supernatural resilience and a bestial fury like no other. Like the fallen Strigoi, the Varghulf will happily devour the dead as well as the living.

