#descr "There is more than one Strigoi to be found leading a petty kingdom of mortals rather than a court of skulking ghouls, for the True Strigoi have kept most of their intellect and have no wish to remain in their fallen state. Amongst these there is one that stands out for his success though, the famed Black Prince of the Border Principalities, the True Strigoi known to his kind as Gashnag. Gashnag was once as other fallen Strigoi, scratching out an existence in the sewers beneath one of the petty city kingdoms of the Borderlands, holding court over nothing more than feral ghouls and rats, but somehow within him the spark of the True Strigoi awakened and gradually he constructed a new identity for himself. Casting himself as a romantic figure, a dashing protector of the innocent tragically cursed and disfigured by dark magic, Gashnag was careful to always conceal his form with a dark cloak and borrowed the manipulative magics of the Lahmians to enhance his own mythos, along with a veritable legion of troubadours paid to spread his carefully constructed tale as far afield as Araby. In time Gashnag came to rule the kingdom in whose shadow he once skulked, saving it from the depradations of other tyrants, of greenskin incursions, and from attacks staged with his own packs of crypt ghouls. The Black Prince has established himself as a stern but fair ruler and is well liked by the smallfolk for the security he brings and swift justice meted out to those who would prey on them. That criminals and troublemakers inevitably vanish is of little concern. Though his route to power is unorthodox Gashnag is sacred to the Strigany people, for he represents a clear path to restore Strigos."
