#descr "Walach Harkon, known to men as Walach the Dark Star, is perhaps the most powerful of all the lineage of Abhorash; indeed it is due to Walach's actions that the bloodline took the common name of the Blood Dragons. Through his centuries of unlife Walach has unfailingly pursued the martial virtues of Abhorash, holding value in himself and others to be defined strictly by honour, pride, prowess, and power, though unlike Abhorash the Dark Star gave no thought to protecting the weak or denying his bloodlust and acknowledged only to those that met his ideals as worthy. Walach's true infamy was gained when he took control of the knightly Imperial fortress of Blood Keep in the Grey Mountains, bested each and every knight there in single combat, slaying those he deemed unworthy and corrupting the remainder with the curse of vampirism. So was founded the vampiric Order of the Blood Dragon, whose reign of terror over a territory crossing both the Empire and Bretonnia lasted for many decades. While the Order was eventually defeated by a vast allied army rallied by Witch Hunters and Sigmarites, Walach and many of his progeny survived and continued their quest to create a new realm ruled by those meeting their standards. As with all members of his bloodline Walach is not so magically gifted as the most powerful members of other vampire families, but he is still a formidable mage and a truly terrifying warrior with centuries of combat experience and near unmatched physical might. In his travels across the world he has secured many magical artifacts, most notably the Crimson Blade which hungrily tears at the flesh of his foes, his blood red armour which protects him from mundane and magical threats alike, and the Blood Chalice which constantly refills with the reinvigorating vital essence of all the greatest fighters Walach has slain. Walach has in recent decades taken to battle atop the reanimated corpse of a great dragon, which he is said to have personally slain."
