#newevent
#msg "Beastlands special mechanics explainer:

No forts: The Beastmen do not use forts at all, and have no fort-only or capital-only recruitables. Resource and recruitment point costs are lower to allow for this. Note that it is still possible to build forts but they will be immediately destroyed! You have no starting fort.

Beastwoods: You will receive a site in every forest province you fully control with positive dominion which grants additional province defence.

Fort and temple destruction: Whenever you successfully storm an enemy fort it will be destroyed immediately and you will be given a random reward and a free temple. (There is no need to order a commander to destroy the fort). Destroying enemy temples gives similar rewards.

Temples: Building a temple will also create a 'weapon pile' site, representing loot offered by the Beastmen, which increases resources. This will last for a random number of turns (7 on average). Your temples also generate Gaves (sacred freespawn), with the chance for them to appear increasing with stronger Dominion.

Ruinous Powers: You may dedicate one of your forest temples in positive dominion to each Chaos God. To do this simply have a Great Bray-Shaman of the respective God visit it to gain a new site offering recruitment of an additional sacred troop."
#header 2 -- use the first line of the event as the header
#nolog
#req_nation 155
#req_owncapital 1
#req_pregame 1 -- only happens before the first turn of the game
#req_fornation 155
#nation 155
#rarity 5
#end



