#descr "Malagor is a legendary figure not only amongst the Beastmen but in the realms of man, where he is known as the Crowfather, the Despoiler of the Sacred, or the Harbinger of Disaster. To the Brayherds he is the doom of men personified, a figure of nightmare revered by all Beastmen and equally feared and reviled by men. To the Cult of Sigmar in particular Malagor is seen as sin incarnate due to his countless blasphemies against the faith and his mere appearance is regarded as perhaps the direst omen possible. From the moment of his birth it was clear that Malagor was favoured by the Chaos Gods, for he possessed a pair of jet black feathered wings and an innate talent for dark magic. While Malagor is a Great Bray-Shaman he does not restrict his counsel to just one Beastlord and instead travels wherever he can further the cause of his kind and the ruin of civilisation, seeing himself as a guide of the Beastmen's inevitable ascendancy. At all times Malagor is focused on casting down the idols of false Gods and shattering the faith of his foes through profane desecration and his ability to extend the dominion of the Beastmen is unmatched. In his gnarled hands Malagor carries a staff hewn from a sacred oak of Athel Loren daubed with filth, blood, and dark glyphs and topped with skeletal human remains made up of bones plundered from the corpses of Bretonnian Grail Knights and Sigmarite priests."
