#name "Norscan King"
#descr "Rulership of Norsca is divided between a fluctuating number of Kings, mighty warleaders who have earned the respect of the Jarls within their domain and show the clear favour of the Ruinous Powers themselves. Kings are the only men capable of uniting the fractious and fiercely independent Norscans tribes into truly huge warhosts capable of sacking well defended cities and potentially conquering entire realms. As such they are able to command the largest Longships capable of carrying the more massive creatures that they might have coerced or forced into service. Most Kings can boast scores of Huskarls personally loyal to them and often powerful forces of Chosen or others favoured by Chaos Undivided gather under their banner, seeing the Kings as instruments of the Ruinous Powers themselves. Norscan Kings ride into battle atop great metal chariots pulled by armoured warbears and arm themselves with magical runic weapons. They are truly awesome combatants, arguably the match of the dreaded Chaos Lords of Slaanesh, Khorne, Nurgle, and Tzeentch. So clearly do they manifest the will of the Ruinous Powers that the Kings are vested with priestly authority recognised by even the most fanatical Shamans. Having reached the pinnacle of Norscan Society each King has only one true goal, to bring such glory to the Ruinous Powers that they will ascend to the status of a Daemon Prince of Chaos Undivided. Many will die before seeing this ambition fulfilled, or be transformed into a Wolfstruck, Bearstruck, or Ravenstruck at the very eve of their ascension, but those that succeed will wield a power nearly umatched in the world of mortals or daemons.

