#descr "Sayl the Faithless, known to some as the Twisted Seer of the Wastes, ia an infamous Kurgan Sorcerer of the Dolgan tribe and their ruler, at least until his long history of betrayals finally forced his escape to the lands of Norsca. Sayl possesses a great mind and a natural talent for both sorcery and deception, qualities which might have assured him a future in the council of some Chaos Lord were Sayl not also a creature of near unequaled hubris and paranoia. Sayl has proclaimed his loyalty to many masters, to Chaos Lords, petty godlings, Daemons, and in his youth the Sorcerer Lord that taught him, but was loyal to none. Sayl was one of four acolytes learning from the famed Schalkain the Vile until he betrayed both his master and his fellows; even now Sayl holds Schalkain's skull as a magical locus in one hand and the twisted betentacled spawn formed from the other three apprentices on the end of his staff. The ritual with which Sayl destroyed the other Sorcerers of the Dolgan tribe and assured his ascent to power burned out his eyes, but Tzeentch, temporarily amused by Sayl's machinations, granted him a hellish vision beyond sight. Sayl might at first be mistaken for an adherent of Chaos Undivided as he serves no individual Ruinous Power, but Faithless in an apt title for the Twisted Seer as the only God he truly recognises is himself.

