#brief "Norsca is a cold and hard land known for its deadly warriors, mighty beasts, and worship of Chaos. Unlike the realms of Slaanesh, Khorne, Nurgle, and Tzeentch the people of Norsca worship the Ruinous Powers in their combined, essential form; Chaos Undivided."
#descr "The mountainous and icy land of Norsca lies to the north of the Empire, across the Sea of Claws, though it casts a shadow across the Old World and beyond. It is a land of hardship and violence, prowled by great beasts mutated by exposure to the energies that constantly radiate from the Chaos Realms of the north pole, but there is no land the Norscans would rather call home. To a Norscan a life of violence and hardship is simply the norm and it is well known that the men of the southern realms are weak and follow false gods precisely because they have not had to earn their life through struggle as a Norscan does. The Norscan tribes follow the way of the warrior, the raider, the champion; they take what they will from those who do not deserve to have it and strive constantly to prove themselves in the eyes of the Ruinous Powers. Norscans recognise Chaos as having four aspects, but they do not worship Slaanesh, Khorne, Nurgle, or Tzeentch, they instead pay tribute to Chaos Undivided exclusively, an oddity which has earned them alliances with the Dragon Ogres and a close relationship with the Everchosen throughout history. Now that the time of awakening has come the Norscans are ready to fill their feared Longships with hardened warriors, unleash the beasts of war, and descend upon the realms of lesser mortals as a storm of destruction."
