#descr "Many think of Nurgle as a purely a force of destruction and misery, but in reality the Plague God is just as capable, and responsible, for healing and growth. Nurgle takes just as much interest in the decline of a plague as he does in its initial growth, for all things are part of the cycle of life and death. So it is that many physicians and healers, frustrated by their inability to cure some particular malady or reach a deeper understanding of mortality may be tempted to turn to Nurgle for knowledge, for cures, and for power. Some of these healers become open worshippers of Nurgle and join a warhost, are discovered and slain as heretics, or are changed into spawn at the whim of the Urfather, but others become covert agents serving the Plague God's agenda. These latter physicians pose as Plague Doctors and truthfully are talented healers of disease, but they are in fact the cause of outbreaks rather than the solution; they journey across the lands joyfully spreading infection for their master and taking pride in its bloom, as well as acting as the eyes and ears of the warhost in foreign lands.

