#descr "Festus the Leechlord, known to some as the Dark Apothecary, others as the Fecundite, is among Grandfather Nurgle's most faithful and beloved servants. Long ago Festus was a physician and alchemist of great renown, the pride of the Imperial university from which he graduated, for it was clear to all that this bright young scholar was a true genius in the science of medicine and furthermore possessed the heart of a true healer, full of compassion and empathy. It was this compassion that led to the fall of Doctor Festus, for when confronted with the Gnashing Fever sweeping Nordland, Festus was unable to accept his failure to save its countless victims. Sleepless, with his mind stretched to breaking by constant unsuccessful attempts to cure the disease, Festus finally fell to his knees and wept, crying out for some higher power to grant him the knowledge to save his fellow man. All at once the patients he was treating turned to face him and spoke with a single ancient voice, promising Festus knowledge of every disease, every cure, should he only pledge his life in service; an offer Festus could not refuse. So was the Leechlord born, as Nurgle filled his mind with impossible knowledge of infinite plagues and equally many possible cures, and Festus, now twisted into a creature of Nurgle, vowed to cure each and every one, no matter how many test subjects he would sadly have to infect in the course of his studies. Festus carries with him at all times his Pestilent Potions that grant regenerative abilities to those around him, a large basket on his back in which he hurls body parts of particular interest, and his loyal medical assistant Glotglot the Nurgling. Clearly favoured by Nurgle, Festus has great priestly authority amongst the followers of the Urfather."
