#descr "Feytor was born to a simple family of farmers in Nordland, near enough the coast to fear Norscan raiders, but not so near to benefit from trade. Life was hard for the family and only became harder when an epidemic ravaged their village, eventually killing so many that Feytor's mother, diseased and half mad, begged any and all Gods to spare her remaining child. Nurgle smiled on the child and so it was that Feytor was spared, the sole survivor, only to find that wherever he tried to find aid he carried the plague, eventually being driven further and further north and finding himself in Norsca. Here, recognised by a Shaman of the Crow Father, Feytor found his calling, swiftly taking over a tribe and becoming a mighty Champion of Nurgle. The child who had once been left lonely and starving, wandering the Empire would now always have company, for he became a carrier of the Zombie Plague and drew the wretches infected with that contagion to his banner in droves. Feytor is the equal of many Chaos Lords of Nurgle but a special fate has been reserved for this servant of the Urfather and he knows he will not see Daemonhood until that fate is discovered and met. In battle Feytor wields a massive glaive known as Nordland's Ruin.

