---- Ku'gath

#newmonster 14667
#spr1 "Sombre_Warhammer/Warhammer_Nurgle/Nurgle_Hero_Kugath.tga"
#spr2 "Sombre_Warhammer/Warhammer_Nurgle/Nurgle_Hero_Kugath2.tga"
#name "Plaguefather"
#descr "Ku'gath, known to most as simply 'Plaguefather', is unique amongst the ranks of Nurgle's Greater Daemons, for he is driven by an eternal quest to discover the perfect pestilence. Ku'gath is so focused on this goal that he cares little for the Great Game between the Chaos Gods, but Nurgle treats his wayward scholar with indulgence nonetheless, for Ku'gath is truly a genius in the art of contagion. The Plaguefather prides himself on his scholarly detachment and is rare to anger; to him mortals and rival Daemons are simply important components in his work rather than enemies to be destroyed. As such he is less powerful magically than his fellows, though he is an excellent researcher. Not wishing to be burdened with the tedium of locomotion, Ku'gath is carried everywhere by a swarm of cackling Nurglings and in battle a number of them will inevitably scamper forward to attack the enemy. Knowing this, Ku'gath keeps his Nurglings coated in a concoction which carries whichever latest plague his taken his interest, so he can record the results and further refine his work. Ku'gath's greatest strength comes from his monomaniacal pursuit of the ultimate contagion; he is currently testing a new plague known as the Bursting Boils, which infects the victim with large pustules that rupture and send a Nurgling springing forth into the world. At present time Bursting Boils is only somewhat contagious and so Ku'gath must sow it in the mortal world himself, but the Plaguefather is surely working to remedy this deficiency. Ku'gath is a frequent and willing visitor to the mortal world and used to extensive travels, so does not become weaker outside Nurgle's Dominion.

[Any province Ku'gath visits which does not already contain a plague of Nurgle will be infected with Bursting Boils]
[Summons 2d6 Pestilent Nurglings on battle start]"
