#name "Nurgle"
#epithet "Children of Joyous Rot"
#sacrificedom
#idealcold 2 -- they come from the polar lands
#color 0.5 0.5 0.3 -- greenish brown
#era 2
#brief "Nurgle is one of the four Ruinous Powers, the Gods of Chaos that draw strength from the darkest mortal emotions and drives. Nurgle is known as the Plague God, Lord of Pestilence, or the Urfather for their domain is disease, decay, destruction, but also rebirth, growth, and fecundity. The followers of Nurgle are many and varied, but all seek esteem in the eyes of Grandfather Nurgle."
#descr "Nurgle is one of the four Ruinous Powers, the Gods of Chaos that draw strength from the darkest mortal emotions and drives. Nurgle is known as the Plague God, Lord of Pestilence, or the Urfather for their domain is disease, decay, destruction, but also rebirth, growth, and fecundity. Each of the Ruinous Powers seeks dominion over the realms of mortals and advantage over their siblings, for to them all life is but a game. Greatest in number of the followers of Nurgle are the Marauders, hardened human warriors from the tribes that surround the Chaos Wastes and are sometimes joined by Ogres or Trolls drawn by the prospect of great reward. Above the Marauders in status are the Chaos Warriors, elite fighters blessed with martial prowess and physical strength, and the Chosen Warriors who show Nurgle's direct favour. Commanding the followers of Nurgle are Champions, Exalted Heroes, and Chaos Lords, each of which seeks to some day ascend to immortality in the form of a Daemon Prince, though most on this path will die in battle or be twisted into a Chaos Spawn by Grandfather Nurgle's blessings. Finally the Daemons of Nurgle are the most direct and loathsome servants of the Plague God, for they are the essence of Nurgle given form and unleashed upon the world."
#summary "Race: Humans with partial cold resistance, beasts of Chaos. Prefer Cold +2. Death scales don't reduce supply.
Military: Exceptional heavy infantry and cavalry, medium infantry, few ranged weapons. Some troops/commanders can earn promotion or transfiguration
Magic: Average. Nature, death, some blood and elemental
Priests: Weak. May blood sacrifice. Dominion increases Death in provinces you don't control. Daemons weaken outside dominion
Mechanics: Plagues that spread, helping you and harming foes"
#flag "Sombre_Warhammer/Warhammer_Nurgle/Nurgle_Flag.tga"
