---- Start of the game message explaining Nurgle's Rot

#newevent
#msg "Nurgle's Rot explainer:

Nurgle's Rot may appear once in the game as a site at a Nurgle controlled province of sufficient population (10k+) with a fort, lab, temple, and positive dominion that is not their capital

Each turn every province adjacent to one infected with the plague has a 16% chance of becoming infected, then an additional 16% chance if a Nurgle Plague Doctor is present

Each turn infected Nurgle controlled provinces have a 10% chance to generate 1d3 death gems and 20% chance to generate 1d3 plaguebearer troops. There is a 5% flat chance the plague will disappear from the province

Each turn infected non-Nurgle provinces have a 5% flat chance to remove the plague, then a 30% chance if the PD is ~15+, then a 6% chance per friendly dominion candle, then a 10% chance if a temple is present, then a 10% chance if a lab is present

If the plague is not removed they will that turn lose 1% population, have 1% of units present diseased, and suffer 5 unrest

There is then a 3% chance of being attacked by Nurgle controlled Plaguebearers led by a Herald

The plague will end everywhere instantly if Nurgle is destroyed."
#header 2 -- use the first line of the event as the header
#nolog
#req_owncapital 1
#req_pregame 1 -- only happens before the first turn of the game
#req_fornation 173
#nation 173
#req_unique 1
#rarity 5
#end




---- Start of the game message explaining Zombie Plague

#newevent
#msg "Zombie Plague explainer:

The Zombie Plague starts as a site at a Nurgle controlled province of sufficient population (10k+) with a fort, lab, temple, and positive dominion that is not their capital

Each turn every province adjacent to one infected with the plague has a 18% chance of becoming infected, then an additional 18% chance if a Nurgle Plague Doctor is present.

Each turn infected Nurgle controlled provinces have a 60% chance to generate 4d6 Plague Zombies at the cost of 10 population. There is a 5% flat chance the plague will disappear from the province.

Each turn infected non-Nurgle provinces have a 5% flat chance to remove the plague, then a 15% chance if there is a fort present, then a 15% chance if the PD is ~10+, then a 35% chance if the PD is ~20+, then a 5% chance if a temple is present, then a 15% chance if a lab is present.

If the plague is not removed they will that turn lose 1% population, have 1% of units present diseased, and suffer 5 unrest.

There is then an 8% chance the province will lose 30 population, suffer 10 unrest, and be attacked by 5d6 Plague Zombies led by a Plague Zombie, controlled by Nurgle.

The plague will end everywhere instantly if Nurgle is destroyed."
#header 2 -- use the first line of the event as the header
#nolog
#req_owncapital 1
#req_pregame 1 -- only happens before the first turn of the game
#req_fornation 173
#nation 173
#req_unique 1
#rarity 5
#end



---- Message explaining Bursting Boils, triggered when Ku'gath appears

#newevent
#msg "Bursting Boils explainer:

Bursting Boils is spread primarily by Ku'gath the Plaguefather and is guaranteed to appear in any province he visits which does not already have a plague of Nurgle.

Each turn every province adjacent to one infected with the plague has a 3% chance of becoming infected, then an additional 3% chance if a Nurgle Plague Doctor is present.

Each turn infected Nurgle controlled provinces have a 20% chance to generate 1d3 nature gems and 100% chance to generate 3d6 Nurglings and lose 10 population. There is a 5% flat chance the plague will disappear from the province.

Each turn infected non-Nurgle provinces have a 5% flat chance to remove the plague, then a 20% chance if a temple is present, then a 30% chance if a lab is present.

If the plague is not removed they will that turn lose 1% population and suffer 10 unrest.

There is then a 5% chance the province will lose 20 population, suffer 15 unrest, and be attacked by 6d6 Nurglings led by a Pestilent Nurgling, controlled by Nurgle.

The plague will end everywhere instantly if Nurgle is destroyed."
#header 2 -- use the first line of the event as the header
#nolog
#req_owncapital 1
#req_fornation 173
#req_mnr 14667 -- Ku'gath must exist
#nation 173
#req_unique 1
#rarity 5
#end



