#descr "While each of the Ruinous Powers by their very nature corrupt the hearts, minds, and souls of mortals, what they offer and those most likely to turn to their gifts vary. Nurgle corrupts those who seek freedom from suffering, Slaanesh seduces with promises of indulgence and sensation, Khorne promises might and glory and vengeance, but Tzeentch offers something purer and more elusive; the Architect of Fate offers the truth. For a mortal man the accumulation of arcane knowledge is necessarily both arduous and partial, and truthfully even the greatest talents have little hope of advancement in more than a single path of study, so the offer of revelation, to even glimpse the greater truths that lie beyond their vision and their lifespan, this is truly tempting. Acolytes of Tzeentch are mortal mages of little talent who have reached beyond their grasp and been blessed with True Sight by the Changer of Ways; in glimpsing the unthinkable they have entered the bondage of the Chaos God in perpetuity and now serve, often covertly, as pieces of Tzeentch's infinite puzzle. Acolytes are adept at disguising their nature and are known to hide their faces behind golden masks even when working together. They are skilled researchers and often pledge themselves to Sorcerers or Sorcerer Lords, acting in support of their superiors."
