---- The Changeling

#newmonster 14842
#spr1 "Sombre_Warhammer/Warhammer_Tzeentch/Tzeentch_Hero_Changeling.tga"
#spr2 "Sombre_Warhammer/Warhammer_Tzeentch/Tzeentch_Hero_Changeling2.tga"
#name "Changeling"
#descr "The nameless Changeling, known also as the Deceiving Horror, or Tzeentch's Trickster was once a mere Herald of Tzeentch but proved itself so gifted in the arts of deception and imitation that Tzeentch granted it the ability to copy perfectly the appearance of others. The Changeling is the ultimate trickster, not only able to take the guise of any other being, but to perfectly imitate their mannerisms and instantly adapt to any situation, casting off suspicion and typically making it fall on innocents. So used to changing form and visage is the Changeling that it is said it no longer even has a true form, though in battle it takes the physical shape of a multi-armed Herald shrouded in a whirling cloak. Though Tzeentch loves to take credit for the Changeling's schemes, only a handful of the Daemon's adventures are carried out at his divine patron's directions. The Great Schemer is content to let the Changeling roam wild through eternity, causing havoc where he may. Each meddling opens up more possibilities in the Great Game, and Tzeentch watches with amusement as the Changeling weaves his uneven tapestry of disruption. That so many of his deceptions have caused terrible wars is of no concern to the Changeling, for the Daemon loves the discord of conflict and the opportunities it brings for deception and dismay. With the coming of the time of strife the Changeling has taken to a more direct approach and begun to simply assassinate key figures in the mortal realms in addition to sowing mischief and paranoia. As a roaming agent of chaos the Changeling does not become weaker outside the dominion of Tzeentch.

