#name "Changer"
#descr "Melekh the Changer was once a blacksmith of the Aesling tribe of Norsca but was set on the path to a new fate when the village Shaman lost control of a spell intended to help his wife give birth safely, killing the woman and ensuring that Melekh's son was born a mutant. Seeing the mutation as a blessing from The Eagle the tribe held a tournament in his honour and when Melekh won, proving himself a great warrior, the Shaman sent him on an impossible quest hoping to prevent any revenge. Melekh was tasked with finding the True Name of Zarechgor, the patron Daemon of the village and so was forced to venture into the Chaos Wastes and eventually to enter the Realm of Tzeentch seeking the knowledge. Melekh battled for years, binding many Daemons of Tzeentch to his will and forming a Daemonic host capable of forcing the Lord of Change to meet him. Though Melekh's force was scattered with little effort by the Greater Daemon, the Chaos Lord was granted a single question for his efforts and in securing the True Name of the Lord of Change he bound a powerful ally to his cause. Upon returning to his tribe Melekh found his son had grown tall and strong and already murdered the Shaman responsible for his mother's death. Free from his task Melekh now seeks only to further the goals of the Architect of Fate, striking down his foes from atop a whirling Disc of Tzeentch and lashing out with lightning, illusion, and fire. Melekh wields a glaive which burns with Blue Fire and wears the famed amulet the Golden Eye of Tzeentch around his neck which grants him near immunity to projectile attacks and protection from lightning. His years spent in the Realm of Chaos have granted him magical power beyond most Chaos Lords of Tzeentch."
