#descr "The Greater Daemons of Tzeentch are known as Lords of Change, Winged Watchers, or Eyes of Tzeentch and they are the most magically powerful and knowledgeable of all Daemons. These birdlike Daemons are master manipulators tasked by the Architect of Fate with directing the course of the mortal world to fit the grand designs of Tzeentch, culminating in their absolute victory in the Great Game of the Ruinous Powers. To gaze into the eye of a Lord of Change would be to see infinite possibility pair with complete, malicious indifference to suffering, to hope, to dreams. Nothing amuses the Lords of Change so much as breaking and remaking the lives of mortals, the fates of entire realms, for to them all of fate is their master's game and they take great pleasure in causing the most change with the subtlest of interventions. That is not to say they are not capable of direct and terrible acts with their considerable sorcerous powers or their significant physical might, for when the will of Tzeentch is challenged their detached nature quickly shifts to spite and anger. In addition to their knowledge of the weave of fate and their great power Lords of Change are also capable of being highly elusive, travelling great distances in secret as a keening zephyr in the winds, a shifting pattern across sand, or a ripple across bodies of water. As with all Daemons they are more powerful within the Dominion of their God and, as Greater Daemons, they are capable of reforming their body should they be slain in this Dominion.

