#descr "Black Orcs are the biggest, meanest, and strongest of all the varieties of Greenskin, a breed that emerged from the east and quickly rose to power across the land. Their name stems from their dark green skin, though it also fits their dour demeaner, for while they are as aggressive and unreasonable as other Orcs, they are grimly and singularly focused on war. The origins of the Black Orcs are a mystery, but one common tale is they were created by the Chaos Dwarfs as battle slaves and nearly doomed that empire when they inevitably revolted. While most Black Orcs either remained in the Dark Lands or migrated west, taking control of many tribes of Orcs and Goblins as they did so, some travelled across the Mountains of Mourn and found themselves in the Eastern Steppe, the domain of the Hobgoblin Khanate. Hobgoblins are loathed by all other Greenskins and held in contempt by Black Orcs, but the Great Horde was simply too powerful and too well adapted to the steppe to successfully war against; additionally the typical Black Orcs method of taking control of tribes through sheer physical might was ineffective against the treacherous and more cunning Hobgoblins. For many decades a stalemate persisted, with Black Orcs slaughtering many Hobgoblins and their Goblin underlings, but slowly being picked off and worn down by the Horde until finally the Hobgobla Khan himself solved the issue by hiring those Black Orcs with enough sense to take the offer as mercenaries and ensuring they would never be short of enemies to fight. Black Orc mercenaries in the east wear lighter armour than many of their western kin and fight with paired choppas. They are fairly few in number for even when generously paid and kept busy making war there aren't many Black Orcs that can stomach working for Hobgoblins, even those as deadly as the Hobgobla Khan.

