#descr "Far to the east of the Old World, beyond the Dark Lands and the Mountains of Mourn, lies the seemingly endless expanse of the Eastern Steppe, the realm of the Hobgobla Khan and the numberless horde of Hobgoblins over which he presides. Hobgoblins are a race smaller and physically weaker than orcs but larger and more aggressive than goblins that are so famed for their treacherous nature that they are despised even by other Greenskins. In the Dark Lands the Hobgoblins have survived the animosity of their kin by serving the Chaos Dwarfs, but across the steppe beyond the Mountains of Mourn they need no such protection, for their Great Horde stands as the undisputed power and can call upon countless Hobgoblins and their swift wolf mounts. So vast and powerful is the Horde that they can handily contest with the horse tribes of Chaos Marauders, are treated with wary caution by the ravenous Ogres, and are known to be the reason for many of the fortifications raised to the north and west of Grand Cathay. While the majority of the Khanate's forces are made up of Hobgoblins they have conquered many goblin tribes which flock to war under their banners and they make use of weapons stolen or traded from the far more advanced civilisations of Zharr-Naggrund and Cathay. Now with the coming of the Awakening God the fractious Horde is ready to sweep across the world like a wave and put all other races under Hobgoblin rule."
