#descr "To the south of the Old World, beyond Tilea and Estalia, across the Great Ocean lies the land of Araby. Araby is in many ways an isolated realm, for to its south lies the brutally inhospitable Great Desert, while to the east are the Lands of the Dead, where the Tomb Kings rule undisputed. However through their impressive trade fleets the people of Araby have long made their presence known to the world, exchanging goods and information with even the High Elves of Ulthuan. Araby is a realm comprised of many City States, each ruled over by a fabulously wealthy and powerful Sultan, and each with its own carefully maintained army. At one time Araby even conquered parts of Estalia and their forces were only stopped by a grand coalition of Old World powers, though while they remain a land of wealth and knowledge it is thought their age of martial glory has passed. The winds of magic blow only weakly in the land of Araby and so the Scholar Mages of the land rely on magical items, broad academic learning, and the binding of capricious magical spirits to keep parity with the wizards of their rival nations. Now with the awakening of the One God the Sultans of Araby have at last united and are poised to unleash their grand armies of mercenaries, tribal warriors, towering elephants, elite guards, and bound Djinn on the wider world."
